{"name":"Cry Me a River","hex":"#427898","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cry me a river","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To weep profusely or excessively in the presence of another person.","To try to obtain the sympathy of another person by complaining or sniveling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cry_me_a_river"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cry Me a River (Arthur Hamilton song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cry Me a River\" is an American popular song, written by Arthur Hamilton, first published in 1953 and made famous in 1955 with the version by Julie London."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Arthur_Hamilton_song)"},{"title":"Cry Me a River (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cry Me a River is an album led by pianist John Hicks, with bassist Dwayne Burno and drummer Victor Lewis."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/JohnHicks_-_Cry_Me_a_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(album)"},{"title":"Cry Me a River (Justin Timberlake song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cry Me a River\" is a song by American singer Justin Timberlake for his debut solo album, Justified (2002). It was thought to be inspired by Timberlake's former relationship with singer Britney Spears. Jive Records released the song to contemporary hit and rhythmic radio in the United States on November 25, 2002, as the album's second single. Accompanied by an electric piano, beatbox, guitars, synthesizers, Arabian-inspired riffs and Gregorian chants, \"Cry Me a River\" is a funk, pop and R&B song about a brokenhearted man who moves on from his past."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Cry_Me_a_River_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Justin_Timberlake_song)"},{"title":"Crying","blocks":[{"text":"Crying is the dropping of tears in response to an emotional state or physical pain. Emotions that can lead to crying include sadness, anger, joy, and fear. Crying can also be caused by relief from a period of stress or anxiety, or as an empathetic response. The act of crying has been defined as \"a complex secretomotor phenomenon characterized by the shedding of tears from the lacrimal apparatus, without any irritation of the ocular structures\", instead, giving a relief which protects from conjunctivitis. A related medical term is lacrimation, which also refers to the non-emotional shedding of tears. Various forms of crying are known as sobbing, weeping, wailing, whimpering, bawling, and blubbering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/330px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crying"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg/250px-Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3d/Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg/250px-Joe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoe_cocker_cry_me_a_river.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Britney_Spears.jpg/500px-Britney_Spears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Britney_Spears.jpg/500px-Britney_Spears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Timberlake acknowledged in December 2011 that the inspiration behind \"Cry Me a River\" was his ended relationship with Britney Spears.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABritney_Spears.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/JT_-_Cry_Me_a_River.png/250px-JT_-_Cry_Me_a_River.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ce/JT_-_Cry_Me_a_River.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/JT_-_Cry_Me_a_River.png/250px-JT_-_Cry_Me_a_River.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Timberlake stalking the blonde woman who portrays Spears inside her house","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJT_-_Cry_Me_a_River.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two women weep at a funeral","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGhanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Tears_.jpg/500px-Tears_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o